<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jagat Raj</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jagat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-raj">Raj</a> was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundela</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> ruler, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrasal">Maharaja Chhatrasal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>. When Chhatrasal died in 1731 his realm was divided between his sons and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a>, and Jagat Raj received the eastern share centred on Jaitpur, while his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hirde-shah">Hirde Sah</a> took Panna. His line held Jaitpur until the British annexed it under the doctrine of lapse in 1849.</p></div>
